    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds solid. one more thing—how do i handle the \"unexpected\" stuff? like, if something totally random happens and they can't deliver, how do i structure the contract so they don't just use it as a loophole to evade their responsibilities or act in bad faith? i want to make sure we aren't left vulnerable to these sneaky, hidden risks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
