      "content": "To prevent bad faith invoke, include a clawback provision that requires the supplier to earn ' Force Majeure' status before you waive delivery penalties. This clause should mandate them to notify you within 24 hours of any disruption and provide verifiable proof of the event. By requiring you to validate their effort to mitigate the issue, you ensure they cannot simply use this clause as a blanket excuse to shift all economic risks onto you.",
      "source": "target",
